function findMedianSortedArrays(nums1, nums2) {
    let merged = [...nums1, ...nums2].sort((a, b) => a - b);
    let len = merged.length;
    let mid = Math.floor(len / 2);

    if (len % 2 === 0) {
        return (merged[mid - 1] + merged[mid]) / 2;
    } else {
        return merged[mid];
    }
}
```

This function first merges the two arrays and sorts them. Then it finds the middle index of the merged array. If the length of the merged array is even, it returns the average of the two numbers at the middle index. If the length is odd, it returns the number at the middle index.

Time complexity: O(n log n), where n is the sum of the lengths of the two input arrays. This is because we are sorting the merged array, which takes O(n log n) time.

Space complexity: O(n), where n is the sum of the lengths of the two input arrays. This is because we are creating a new array to merge the two input arrays.

