query:
Let \[f(x) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl} x^2-4 & \text{ if }x < 7, \\
x-13 & \text{ if } x \geq 7.
\end{array}
\right.\] What is $f(f(f(17)))$?

response:
First, we find $f(17)$:

\[f(17) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl}
17^2 - 4 & \text{ if } 17 < 7, \\
17 - 13 & \text{ if } 17 \geq 7.
\end{array}
\right.\]

Since $17 \geq 7$, we have $f(17) = 17 - 13 = 4$.

Next, we find $f(4)$:

\[f(4) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl}
4^2 - 4 & \text{ if } 4 < 7, \\
4 - 13 & \text{ if } 4 \geq 7.
\end{array}
\right.\]

Since $4 < 7$, we have $f(4) = 4^2 - 4 = 16 - 4 = 12$.

Finally, we find $f(12)$:

\[f(12) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl}
12^2 - 4 & \text{ if } 12 < 7, \\
12 - 13 & \text{ if } 12 \geq 7.
\end{array}
\right.\]

Since $12 \geq 7$, we have $f(12) = 12 - 13 = -1$.

Therefore, $f(f(f(17))) = -1$.

